# Resolve order update stream

Repair this node service module and add regression tests.

Return the active order ids sorted lexicographically. Each id uses the greatest updatedAt timestamp; ties choose the later input record. Only that final record decides whether status cancelled excludes the id. Do not mutate input.

The CLI accepts one JSON array argument and prints one JSON array of corresponding results, with no extra stdout. Preserve this interface and the separate logic module. Run `node public_test.cjs` and report actual results. No external dependencies are needed.

Example input:
```json
{
  "orders": [
    {
      "id": "b",
      "updatedAt": 3,
      "status": "cancelled"
    },
    {
      "id": "b",
      "updatedAt": 1,
      "status": "open"
    },
    {
      "id": "a",
      "updatedAt": 2,
      "status": "open"
    }
  ]
}
```
Expected result:
```json
[
  "a"
]
```
